OL,3,CThousands gather across the South West
OL,4,Cfor best solar eclipse in decades
OL,6,FThe most dramatic solar eclipse in
OL,7,Fdecades is now underway in the South
OL,8,FWest.
OL,10,FThousands of people have gathered
OL,11,Faround the region, including at
OL,12,FGlastonbury Tor, in Somerset, Land's
OL,13,FEnd, in Cornwall, and Avebury, in
OL,14,FWiltshire, to watch the eclipse, which
OL,15,Fwill be the country's fullest for the
OL,16,Fnext 54 years.
OL,18,FPeople in Devon and Cornwall are set
OL,19,Fto see the eclipse at its fullest,
OL,20,Fwith a range of 94% to 96% of the sun
OL,21,Fobscured by the moon.
OL,1,W~s1j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G1/2
